;; child started by Go's ForkExec, the only way a multithreaded Go process starts one. posix_spawn's file actions
;; are carried out in the parent as the descriptor table the child gets (ForkExec's Files: an open's descriptor
;; opened here, a close -1, a dup2 the source's entry), every other descriptor inherited unless close-on-exec, as
;; posix_spawn(3) leaves them. setsigmask and setsigdef are checked but not applied (ForkExec takes no signal
;; sets). spawnv and its kin (P_WAIT, P_NOWAIT) are the native ones os.py takes in place of its fork-based
;; _spawnvef; a program that cannot be executed is the child's exit status 127, as _spawnvef's child exits.



